# <type>(<scope>)!: <subject>                                      <- at most 72 characters, imperative, lower case, no period
#
# Why this change, what it does differently (wrap at about 72 columns). The body is optional;
# leave the empty line above it.
#
# Footers (optional):
#   BREAKING CHANGE: <what breaks and how to migrate>
#   Refs: #123
#
# Types: feat fix perf refactor docs test build ci chore style revert
#   feat      a new feature for users                  (minor release)    fix    a bug fix                (patch)
#   perf      a performance improvement                (patch)            docs   documentation only
#   refactor  code change that neither fixes nor adds   test   tests only        build  build, packaging, dependencies
#   ci        workflows and CI scripts                  chore  maintenance        style  formatting only
#   revert    undoes an earlier commit
# A "!" after the type or scope, or a BREAKING CHANGE footer, marks a breaking change (while the version is 0.x: a minor release).
# Scopes are free: gui, core, prefs, lab, packaging, deps ...
#
# Examples:
#   feat(gui): add a dark appearance to the preferences window
#   fix: keep the window on the screen that holds the cursor
#   refactor(core)!: rename the snippets store
#
# Lines starting with # are removed by git. Enable this template once, in your clone only:
#   git config commit.template .gitmessage
